{"title":"Career Roadmap · Database Executive","role":"Database Executive","summary":"A Database Executive supports the storage, organisation, maintenance, security and retrieval of organisational data. The role typically involves database operations, SQL queries, data quality, backups, reporting and basic database administration.","facts":{"Current degree":"BCA (Bachelor of Computer Applications)","Course":"General BCA"},"about":[{"label":"Career note","text":"“Database Executive” is generally an entry-level or operations-oriented title. With stronger SQL, database administration, cloud and automation skills, the career can progress into DBA, Database Engineer or Data Platform roles."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus","What to Build"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2028"},{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"DBMS, SQL, programming, data modelling"}],[{"text":"2028–2030"},{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Database operations, reporting, data quality"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Professional"},{"text":"Administration, performance, backup/recovery"}],[{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Cloud databases, automation, security"}],[{"text":"2037–2040"},{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Database architecture and data platforms"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Strategic"},{"text":"Cloud data infrastructure, AI/data platforms"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Key Skills","Proof"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Programming + DBMS fundamentals"},{"text":"SQL, relational concepts, Python/Java"},{"text":"SQL projects"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Database development"},{"text":"Queries, joins, procedures, data modelling"},{"text":"Database application"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Administration"},{"text":"Backup, security, performance, Linux"},{"text":"DBA project + internship"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Production skills"},{"text":"Cloud DB, automation, monitoring, HA"},{"text":"Production-style database project"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Database Fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"DBMS Concepts"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Database"},{"text":"DBMS"},{"text":"RDBMS"},{"text":"Tables"},{"text":"Rows"},{"text":"Columns"},{"text":"Primary keys"},{"text":"Foreign keys"},{"text":"Constraints"},{"text":"Relationships"},{"text":"Indexes"},{"text":"Views"},{"text":"Transactions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Application","Database","Query","Data","Response"]},{"type":"h","text":"SQL — Core Skill"},{"type":"p","text":"Become highly comfortable with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic SQL"},{"type":"p","text":"SELECT"},{"type":"p","text":"INSERT"},{"type":"p","text":"UPDATE"},{"type":"p","text":"DELETE"},{"type":"h","text":"Filtering"},{"type":"p","text":"WHERE"},{"type":"p","text":"ORDER BY"},{"type":"p","text":"GROUP BY"},{"type":"p","text":"HAVING"},{"type":"h","text":"Joins"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"INNER JOIN"},{"text":"LEFT JOIN"},{"text":"RIGHT JOIN"},{"text":"FULL OUTER JOIN"},{"text":"SELF JOIN"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced SQL"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Subqueries"},{"text":"CTEs"},{"text":"Window functions"},{"text":"CASE"},{"text":"Aggregate functions"},{"text":"Set operations"},{"text":"Views"},{"text":"Stored procedures"},{"text":"Functions"},{"text":"Triggers"}]},{"type":"p","text":"SQL should become one of the student's strongest technical skills."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Relational Database Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ER diagrams"},{"text":"Entity relationships"},{"text":"Cardinality"},{"text":"Normalisation"},{"text":"Denormalisation"},{"text":"Functional dependencies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Requirements","ER Model","Schema","Tables","Constraints","Queries"]},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"1NF"},{"text":"2NF"},{"text":"3NF"},{"text":"BCNF concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Databases"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MySQL"},{"text":"PostgreSQL"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then become familiar with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microsoft SQL Server"},{"text":"Oracle Database"}]},{"type":"p","text":"You do not need to master every database. One relational database deeply + familiarity with others is a better strategy."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Database Development"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced SQL"},{"type":"p","text":"Build practical ability in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Complex joins"},{"text":"CTEs"},{"text":"Window functions"},{"text":"Query optimisation"},{"text":"Transactions"},{"text":"Stored procedures"},{"text":"Views"},{"text":"Data validation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example problem"},{"type":"p","text":"Given:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Customers","Orders","Products","Payments"]},{"type":"p","text":"Answer:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Top customers"},{"text":"Monthly revenue"},{"text":"Repeat customers"},{"text":"Unpaid orders"},{"text":"Average order value"},{"text":"Product performance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Database Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Connect applications to databases using:"},{"type":"h","text":"Java"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"JDBC"},{"text":"Connection pooling"},{"text":"Prepared statements"},{"text":"Transactions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"psycopg"},{"text":"SQLAlchemy"},{"text":"Database APIs"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Application","API","Database","Query","Result"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Data Quality"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Duplicate records"},{"text":"Missing values"},{"text":"Invalid values"},{"text":"Inconsistent formats"},{"text":"Referential-integrity problems"},{"text":"Incorrect timestamps"},{"text":"Duplicate transactions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop data-cleaning SQL scripts."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Database Administration"},{"type":"p","text":"This is where the student moves from SQL developer → database operations professional."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"User Management"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Users"},{"text":"Roles"},{"text":"Permissions"},{"text":"Privileges"},{"text":"Authentication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Backup & Recovery"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Full backup"},{"text":"Incremental backup"},{"text":"Differential backup"},{"text":"Point-in-time recovery"},{"text":"Restore testing"},{"text":"Recovery objectives"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important concepts:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"RPO"},{"text":"RTO"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A backup that has never been successfully restored should not be treated as a proven recovery strategy."},{"type":"h","text":"Database Performance"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Indexing"},{"text":"Query plans"},{"text":"Execution plans"},{"text":"Slow queries"},{"text":"Table statistics"},{"text":"Partitioning concepts"},{"text":"Connection pooling"},{"text":"Locking"},{"text":"Blocking"},{"text":"Deadlocks"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the principle:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Slow application","Investigate query","Examine execution plan","Identify bottleneck","Optimise","Measure again"]},{"type":"h","text":"Linux Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"For database operations, learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linux filesystem"},{"text":"Permissions"},{"text":"Processes"},{"text":"Services"},{"text":"Logs"},{"text":"SSH"},{"text":"Shell commands"},{"text":"Cron"},{"text":"Disk monitoring"},{"text":"Memory/CPU monitoring"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Basic shell scripting is highly useful."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Data